  "slug": "genetic-effects-1a8b",
  "summary": "Six preprints extend variant-to-gene mapping beyond expression eQTLs to splicing, structural variants, and single-variant perturbation in disease tissues.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is assigning disease-associated noncoding variants to effector genes within relevant tissue or cell contexts, with several studies looking beyond total gene abundance. In IBD colon samples (1,149), joint eQTL and sQTL mapping identifies colocalized expression and splicing effects, implicating NMD and immune pathways. For type 2 diabetes, 338 fine-mapped signals are colocalized with adipose expression, splicing and transcript usage, and CELL-X uses islet single-cell data to prioritize beta cells and genes such as SLC30A8 and TCF7L2. Pangenome genotyping in CARTaGENE adds 103 SV-eQTLs. MPRA and CRISPR perturbation in chondrocytes link rs1895062 to PAPPA in osteoarthritis. The IGVF Catalog integrates 657 datasets as supporting infrastructure.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
